# Cyrius Field Notes — Language Gotchas (platform & ABI)
# Per-OS preprocessor target flags, struct return by value, variadic fns,
# the fncall6-into-extern-C arg-count ceiling, AArch64 cross-`bl`
# register clobber + immediate-encoding limits, and the agnos
# two-sided ABI syscall-wrapper mirror, plus the aarch64 private-alias
# band and the Darwin AT_* flag divergence.
# Refreshed 2026-08-07 at v6.5.10: added the aarch64 ≥1000 private-alias
# band + the Darwin AT_* divergence from v6.5.7 — the release where ONE
# cross-OS test finally RUN on ecb / ach turned up seven wrapper defects
# that five targets' worth of compile-only checks could not see.
# ⚠ v6.6.1: the `vr01_` FILENAME PREFIX this file used to name was RETIRED at
# v6.5.11. The cross-OS selector is now the `tests/tcyr/crossos/` DIRECTORY, so a
# file named `vr01_*` today silently OPTS OUT of the release gate's cross-OS leg —
# the exact opposite of what the prefix used to mean.
# Prior refresh 2026-07-27 at v6.4.82: `fncall6_ceiling_into_extern_c`
# carries a premise-check banner — it predates the v6.4.64 Win64
# stack-arg codegen fix, and PURE cyrius has no arity limit at all
# (5-20 args verified on real hardware). A rule that tells you to
# restructure code around codegen is a bug report, not a rule.
# 6.7.10: the raw-asm exit is per OS (INTO raw_syscall_numbers_on_aarch64_and_the_darwin_at_flag_divergence);
# still 16 entries.
# 16 entries (re-DERIVED at 6.6.16 after one: the IOCP-as-a-wake-slot entry; the other 6.6.16
# notes went INTO existing entries — CYRIUS-2026-0025 + four test traps into the SIGPIPE class, accept's
# inherited non-blocking mode and the Win64 eax mask into the Winsock entry, the agnos decline
# stub into agnos_two_sided_abi_mirror).
# v6.7.11: +4 entries — dce_compaction_moves_a_kernels_data_v6711, cyrius_header_return_types_and_agnos_hosts_v6711,
# open_a_directory_you_will_list_with_o_directory_v6711, tagged_handles_exact_ranges_and_time_bounds_where_zero_means_
